# rp2350_touch_lcd_154

A Waveshare RP2350-Touch-LCD-1.54: an RP2350A with 16MB of flash carrying a
240 by 240 IPS panel on an ST7789 over four-wire SPI, a CST816 capacitive
touch controller, and a QMI8658 inertial sensor.

It derives from pico2-arm because that is what it is: the same RP2350A the Pico
SDK configures as pico2. The SDK publishes no board header for this product,
and Waveshare's own firmware for it selects PICO_BOARD pico2 and drives every
peripheral by explicit GPIO number, which is exactly what deriving does here.
The chip, the SDK, and the ABI come from the base; the three bindings above
and the pin maps in the providers are what this board adds.

The panel is wired to SPI1 and the two I2C devices share I2C1.

**The pin assignments in the providers are taken from Waveshare's public
firmware repository for this product, not from a schematic, because the wiki
refuses automated requests. They must be confirmed against the schematic
before this board is trusted with hardware.**

https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/RP2350-Touch-LCD-1.54
